  {
   "id": "cOaVo8e6AAAJ",
   "from": "Paul Buerkner",
   "author": "6e3dd74b422c061b",
   "date": "2018-03-29T16:24:02Z",
   "subject": "Re: [brms-users] Reparametrization of gamma distribution",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Currently, vectorization is not implemented and is hard to do in general as user-defined Stan functions cannot be overloaded (that is differnet function signatures defined on the same function name). If I get a good idea how to allow vectorization, I will implement it.<br></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">2018-03-29 16:25 GMT+02:00 Lucas Deschamps <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">lucas.de...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span>:<br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">I&#39;m actually trying your wonderful new function, and a question appears : did you implement a way to vectorize the sampling statement? The resulting code is now : <div><br><div><pre style=\"font-family:&quot;Ubuntu Mono&quot;;outline:none;border-width:initial;border-style:none;word-break:break-all;line-height:19px;color:rgb(230,225,220);font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;background-color:rgb(28,28,28);font-size:12.4pt!important;white-space:pre-wrap!important\"><span style=\"outline:none;border-width:initial;border-style:none;word-break:break-all\">  // likelihood including all constants \r\n  if (!prior_only) { \r\n    for (n in 1:N) { \r\n      target += gamma2_lpdf(Y[n] | mu[n], phi); \r\n    } \r\n  } </span></pre><div><br></div>Which is known to be slower. But I can guess that to ensure compatibility with all possible strange distributions, it is simpler to use a loop!</div><div><br></div><div>Anyway, great job!</div><div></div></div></div></blockquote></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div><br>Le jeudi 29 mars 2018 06:06:00 UTC-4, Paul Buerkner a écrit :</div></div></div></blockquote></div></div>"
    ],
